Nim Game AI – Game Search
1. Abstract
Nim is a mathematical strategy game in which players remove objects from one or more piles. This project develops an AI agent that plays Nim optimally using game-search techniques such as Minimax and the theory of Grundy numbers. The AI analyzes the current game state, identifies winning and losing positions, and selects the best possible move. The system demonstrates how artificial intelligence can use mathematical reasoning to guarantee a win whenever a winning strategy exists.
2. Introduction
Artificial Intelligence enables computers to make decisions and solve problems intelligently. Game-playing AI is an important application of AI because it involves decision-making, search, and strategy.
Nim is a two-player game where players take turns removing one or more objects from a single pile. The player who removes the last object wins. In this project, an AI agent is designed to play Nim optimally by analyzing possible moves and applying the mathematical concept of Grundy numbers or the Minimax algorithm.
3. Problem Statement
Develop an AI-based Nim game player that can analyze the current game state, determine whether it is a winning or losing position, and select an optimal move. The AI should use game-search techniques or Grundy number theory to ensure that it wins from every possible winning position when the opponent plays optimally.
4. Objectives
To develop an AI agent that plays Nim optimally.
To represent the game using states and possible actions.
To apply Minimax or Grundy number theory for decision-making.
To identify winning and losing game positions.
To select the best move from every winning position.
To demonstrate the mathematical theory behind optimal Nim play.
To provide an interactive game between the user and the AI.
